# Heat Exchanger & Fluid Mechanics Analysis

**Course:** Thermal Fluids & Fluid Mechanics  
**Topic:** Dual Centrifugal Pump Station Design & Performance Analysis  

---

## Executive Summary & System Overview

This project evaluated pump affinity laws, hydraulic head loss, and parallel network configurations to design a dual centrifugal pump station capable of meeting a variable client demand of $6\text{ to }780\text{ ltr/min}$ against a constant $5\text{ m}$ system head constraint[cite: 7].

### Key Technical Achievements & Analysis:
* **Parallel Pump Configuration:** Engineered a solution combining Pump C ($D = 200\text{ mm}$) and Pump D ($D = 250\text{ mm}$) in parallel at $2900\text{ RPM}$, achieving a combined maximum flow rate of $1064\text{ ltr/min}$ at $5\text{ m}$ head[cite: 7].
* **No-Electronics Constraint:** Integrated non-return check valves (NRVs), a manual globe valve for throttling, and a mechanical rotameter for visual flow verification without electronic instrumentation[cite: 7].
* **Dimensional Scaling & Affinity Laws:** Applied scaling principles to extrapolate experimental laboratory data across variable rotational speeds ($2100\text{ to }3300\text{ RPM}$) to standard operating conditions ($2900\text{ RPM}$)[cite: 7].

